{%- comment -%}
  LETS purchase options app block — the storefront BUY area for a product page.

  The merchant drops "LETS Subscribe & Save" onto the product page in the theme
  editor and it ALWAYS renders a working buy area, in one of two shapes:

    - the product HAS published subscription plans → the two-card chooser:
      a highlighted subscription card (price, saving badge, benefit list, an
      optional "Read more", an optional free-gift row, and a cadence picker when
      more than one plan exists) above a plain "Purchase once" card;
    - the product has NO subscription plans → the one-time card alone.

  So the block can be placed on every product page once and it never leaves a
  page with a dead area: publishing a plan later (LETS admin → Products → a plan
  → "Publish to Shopify") turns the same block into the chooser, with no theme
  edit.

  Subscriptions render from Shopify's NATIVE selling_plan_allocations — the
  groups our app publishes. That is what makes the Shopify-Payments rail work
  end to end: the cart line carries a selling_plan id, so Shopify's checkout
  vaults the card and creates a SubscriptionContract our app owns (and then
  bills, cycle by cycle, from BillingAttemptJob). No App Proxy call is involved,
  so the storefront can never be talked into a price we did not publish.

  EVERY colour and string below is a theme-editor setting; nothing is hardcoded
  to a brand. Prices, cadence names and the saving percentage come from Shopify
  and are NOT editable — they are what the shopper will actually be charged.

  For DEPOSIT + installments (the PayPlus rail) use the sibling block
  "LETS Deposit Plan" (blocks/installments_button.liquid) instead — that rail
  charges a PayPlus token and has its own App-Proxy-signed flow.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  selected_or_first_available_variant is NIL when every variant is sold out (and
  the product does not continue selling), which would render the whole block as
  nothing — indistinguishable, to a merchant, from "the app is broken". Fall back
  to the first variant so the block always has something to price, and let the
  sold-out state below disable the button honestly.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first -%}
{%- assign allocations = current_variant.selling_plan_allocations -%}
{%- assign has_plans = false -%}
{%- if allocations != blank and allocations.size > 0 -%}
  {%- assign has_plans = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if product and current_variant -%}
  {%- comment -%} The cheapest allocation leads the card (the best offer wins). {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign lead = allocations | sort: 'per_delivery_price' | first -%}
  {%- assign sub_price = lead.per_delivery_price -%}
  {%- assign one_time_price = current_variant.price -%}

  {%- assign saves = false -%}
  {%- if has_plans and sub_price < one_time_price -%}
    {%- assign saves = true -%}
    {%- assign saved_pct = one_time_price | minus: sub_price | times: 100.00 | divided_by: one_time_price | round -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- assign subscribe_first = true -%}
  {%- if block.settings.default_selection == 'onetime' or has_plans == false -%}
    {%- assign subscribe_first = false -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="lets-po" data-lets-po data-lets-po-after="{{ block.settings.after_add | default: 'stay' }}">
    <form method="post" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" data-lets-po-form>
      <input type="hidden" name="form_type" value="product">
      <input type="hidden" name="utf8" value="✓">
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current_variant.id }}" data-lets-po-variant>

      {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <p class="lets-po__heading">{{ block.settings.heading }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if has_plans -%}
        {%- comment -%} ---------- The subscription card ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="lets-po__card lets-po__card--sub{% if subscribe_first %} is-selected{% endif %}" data-lets-po-card="subscribe">
          <label class="lets-po__head">
            <input type="radio" class="lets-po__radio" name="lets_purchase_type" value="subscribe"
              data-lets-po-type {% if subscribe_first %}checked{% endif %}>
            <span class="lets-po__title">{{ block.settings.subscribe_label | default: 'Subscribe & save' }}</span>

            {%- if block.settings.badge_text != blank -%}
              <span class="lets-po__badge">{{ block.settings.badge_text }}</span>
            {%- elsif saves -%}
              <span class="lets-po__badge">{{ saved_pct }}% {{ block.settings.badge_off_word | default: 'OFF' }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}

            <span class="lets-po__prices">
              <span class="lets-po__price">{{ sub_price | money }}</span>
              {%- if saves -%}
                <s class="lets-po__compare">{{ one_time_price | money }}</s>
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
          </label>

          <div class="lets-po__body" data-lets-po-body {% unless subscribe_first %}hidden{% endunless %}>
            <div class="lets-po__rule"></div>

            <div class="lets-po__benefits-row">
              <ul class="lets-po__benefits">
                {%- comment -%}
                  The first benefit falls back to the PLAN'S OWN cadence name, so
                  the card is never wrong about how often the shopper is billed
                  even if the merchant leaves the field empty.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <li class="lets-po__benefit">{{ block.settings.benefit_1 | default: lead.selling_plan.name }}</li>
                {%- if block.settings.benefit_2 != blank -%}
                  <li class="lets-po__benefit">{{ block.settings.benefit_2 }}</li>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.settings.benefit_3 != blank -%}
                  <li class="lets-po__benefit">{{ block.settings.benefit_3 }}</li>
                {%- endif -%}
              </ul>

              {%- if block.settings.more_body != blank -%}
                <button type="button" class="lets-po__more-toggle" data-lets-po-more
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="lets-po-more">
                  <span>{{ block.settings.more_label | default: 'Read more' }}</span>
                  <svg class="lets-po__chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M5 7.5 10 12.5 15 7.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
                      stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                  </svg>
                </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            {%- if block.settings.more_body != blank -%}
              <div class="lets-po__more-body" id="lets-po-more" hidden>{{ block.settings.more_body }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Cadence — only when there is a real choice to make. The option value
              IS the selling_plan id Shopify expects, so what the shopper picks is
              exactly what gets billed.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if allocations.size > 1 -%}
              <div class="lets-po__cadence">
                <label class="lets-po__cadence-label" for="lets-po-plan">
                  {{ block.settings.cadence_label | default: 'Delivery every' }}
                </label>
                <select id="lets-po-plan" name="selling_plan" class="lets-po__select" data-lets-po-select>
                  {%- for allocation in allocations -%}
                    <option value="{{ allocation.selling_plan.id }}"
                      data-price="{{ allocation.per_delivery_price | money }}"
                      {% if allocation.selling_plan.id == lead.selling_plan.id %}selected{% endif %}>
                      {{ allocation.selling_plan.name }} — {{ allocation.per_delivery_price | money }}
                    </option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- else -%}
              <input type="hidden" name="selling_plan" value="{{ lead.selling_plan.id }}" data-lets-po-select>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if block.settings.gift_text != blank -%}
              <div class="lets-po__rule"></div>
              <div class="lets-po__gift">
                {%- if block.settings.gift_image != blank -%}
                  <img class="lets-po__gift-img"
                    src="{{ block.settings.gift_image | image_url: width: 240 }}"
                    alt="{{ block.settings.gift_tag | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120">
                {%- endif -%}
                <div class="lets-po__gift-copy">
                  {%- if block.settings.gift_tag != blank -%}
                    <span class="lets-po__gift-tag">{{ block.settings.gift_tag }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <p class="lets-po__gift-text">{{ block.settings.gift_text }}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="lets-po__gift-prices">
                  <span class="lets-po__gift-free">{{ block.settings.gift_free_label | default: 'FREE' }}</span>
                  {%- if block.settings.gift_value != blank -%}
                    <s class="lets-po__compare">{{ block.settings.gift_value }}</s>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} ---------- The one-time card (always present) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="lets-po__card{% unless subscribe_first %} is-selected{% endunless %}" data-lets-po-card="onetime">
        <label class="lets-po__head">
          {%- if has_plans -%}
            <input type="radio" class="lets-po__radio" name="lets_purchase_type" value="onetime"
              data-lets-po-type {% unless subscribe_first %}checked{% endunless %}>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="lets-po__title">{{ block.settings.one_time_label | default: 'Purchase once' }}</span>
          <span class="lets-po__prices">
            <span class="lets-po__price">{{ one_time_price | money }}</span>
          </span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <button type="submit" class="lets-po__cta" data-lets-po-cta {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
        {%- if current_variant.available -%}
          <span>{{ block.settings.button_label | default: 'Add to cart' }}</span>
          {%- if block.settings.show_price_in_button -%}
            <span class="lets-po__cta-price" data-lets-po-cta-price
              data-sub-price="{{ sub_price | money }}"
              data-onetime-price="{{ one_time_price | money }}">
              {%- if subscribe_first -%}{{ sub_price | money }}{%- else -%}{{ one_time_price | money }}{%- endif -%}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <span>{{ block.settings.sold_out_label | default: 'Sold out' }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </button>

      {%- if request.design_mode and has_plans == false -%}
        {%- comment -%} Theme-editor-only hint; shoppers never see this. {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="lets-po__hint">
          {{ 'LETS: no subscription plan is published for this product yet, so this block shows a one-time purchase only. In the LETS app: Products → this product → a subscription plan → "Publish to Shopify".' }}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </form>
  </div>

  {%- style -%}
    /* THEME-FIRST by default. Every colour below falls back to the theme's own
       text colour (currentColor) or to transparent, and every size is relative
       (em), so the block inherits the surrounding product page — its font, its
       ink, its scale. A merchant only overrides what they explicitly want to
       differ; leaving a colour setting empty means "use the theme's". */
    .lets-po {
      --lets-accent: {{ block.settings.accent_color | default: 'currentColor' }};
      --lets-card: {{ block.settings.card_bg | default: 'transparent' }};
      --lets-border: {{ block.settings.border_color | default: 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent)' }};
      --lets-ink: {{ block.settings.text_color | default: 'inherit' }};
      --lets-ink-strong: {{ block.settings.title_color | default: 'inherit' }};
      --lets-muted: {{ block.settings.muted_color | default: 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent)' }};
      --lets-radius: {{ block.settings.corner_radius | default: 0 }}px;
      /* The button reads as the theme's own emphasis unless overridden: ink fill,
         page-coloured label — the pairing that matches most themes' primary CTA. */
      --lets-cta-bg: {{ block.settings.button_bg | default: 'currentColor' }};
      --lets-cta-fg: {{ block.settings.button_fg | default: 'Canvas' }};
      margin: 1em 0;
      font-family: inherit;
      color: var(--lets-ink);
    }
    .lets-po__heading { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.6em; color: var(--lets-ink-strong); }

    .lets-po__card {
      background: var(--lets-card);
      border: 1px solid var(--lets-border);
      border-radius: var(--lets-radius);
      margin-bottom: 0.6em;
    }
    /* Selection is shown by WEIGHT, not by a brand colour: a thicker border in
       the theme's own ink reads as "chosen" in any palette. */
    .lets-po__card.is-selected { border: 2px solid var(--lets-accent); }
    .lets-po__card--sub.is-selected .lets-po__title { color: var(--lets-ink-strong); }

    .lets-po__head {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6em;
      padding: 0.9em 1em; cursor: pointer; margin: 0;
    }
    .lets-po__title {
      font-size: 1.05em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .01em;
      color: var(--lets-ink-strong);
    }
    .lets-po__prices { margin-inline-start: auto; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5em; }
    .lets-po__price { font-size: 1.1em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--lets-ink-strong); }
    .lets-po__compare { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--lets-muted); }

    /* Radio: a ring that fills with the accent when chosen. `--lets-card` is the
       hole's colour, so on a transparent (theme-inherited) card the fill uses the
       page behind it instead of punching a white dot into a dark theme. */
    .lets-po__radio {
      appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
      inline-size: 1.15em; block-size: 1.15em; flex: none; margin: 0; cursor: pointer;
      border: 2px solid var(--lets-muted); border-radius: 50%;
      background: transparent;
    }
    .lets-po__radio:checked {
      border-color: var(--lets-accent);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at center,
          var(--lets-accent) 0 0.3em,
          transparent 0.3em);
    }
    .lets-po__radio:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--lets-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }

    .lets-po__badge {
      background: var(--lets-accent);
      color: {{ block.settings.badge_text_color | default: 'Canvas' }};
      font-size: 0.75em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 0.35em 0.7em; border-radius: var(--lets-radius); white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .lets-po__body { padding: 0 1em 0.9em; }
    .lets-po__rule { border-top: 1px dashed var(--lets-border); margin: 0.2em 0 0.8em; }

    .lets-po__benefits-row { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.75em; }
    .lets-po__benefits { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; flex: 1; }
    .lets-po__benefit {
      position: relative; padding-inline-start: 1.6em; margin-bottom: 0.45em;
      font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.45;
    }
    /* The check is drawn, not an icon font — nothing to load, nothing to break.
       PHYSICAL borders on purpose: a checkmark must not mirror in RTL (logical
       ones turned it into a ">" chevron on a Hebrew storefront). */
    .lets-po__benefit::before {
      content: ''; position: absolute; inset-inline-start: 0.15em; inset-block-start: 0.35em;
      inline-size: 0.55em; block-size: 0.3em;
      border-left: 2px solid var(--lets-accent);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--lets-accent);
      transform: rotate(-45deg);
    }

    .lets-po__more-toggle {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.25em; cursor: pointer;
      background: none; border: 0; padding: 0; font: inherit; font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--lets-accent); text-decoration: underline;
    }
    .lets-po__chevron { inline-size: 1.1em; block-size: 1.1em; transition: transform .2s ease; }
    .lets-po__more-toggle[aria-expanded="true"] .lets-po__chevron { transform: rotate(180deg); }
    .lets-po__more-body { font-size: 0.9em; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0.6em; }

    .lets-po__cadence { margin-top: 0.9em; }
    .lets-po__cadence-label { display: block; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.35em; }
    .lets-po__select {
      width: 100%; padding: 0.6em 0.7em; font: inherit; color: inherit;
      background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--lets-border); border-radius: var(--lets-radius);
    }

    .lets-po__gift { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.9em; }
    .lets-po__gift-img { inline-size: 5em; block-size: auto; flex: none; object-fit: contain; }
    .lets-po__gift-copy { flex: 1; }
    .lets-po__gift-tag {
      display: inline-block;
      background: {{ block.settings.gift_tag_bg | default: 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 65%, transparent)' }};
      color: {{ block.settings.gift_tag_color | default: 'Canvas' }};
      font-size: 0.75em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 0.35em 0.7em; border-radius: var(--lets-radius); margin-bottom: 0.5em;
    }
    .lets-po__gift-text { font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.45; margin: 0; }
    .lets-po__gift-prices { text-align: end; white-space: nowrap; }
    .lets-po__gift-free { font-size: 0.95em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--lets-accent); margin-inline-end: 0.4em; }

    .lets-po__cta {
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.6em;
      width: 100%; cursor: pointer; margin-top: 0.4em;
      padding: 1em 1.2em; border: 0; border-radius: var(--lets-radius);
      background: var(--lets-cta-bg);
      color: var(--lets-cta-fg);
      font-family: inherit; font-size: 1em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .lets-po__cta[disabled] { opacity: .5; cursor: not-allowed; }
    /* Confirmation for themes with no cart drawer to open — the shopper stayed
       on the page, so the button itself has to say the line was added. */
    .lets-po__cta[data-lets-added]::after {
      content: '✓';
      font-size: 1.1em;
    }
    .lets-po__hint { font-size: 0.8em; opacity: .75; margin: 0.6em 0 0; }
  {%- endstyle -%}

  <script>
    (function () {
      'use strict';
      var root = document.querySelector('[data-lets-po]');
      if (!root || root.dataset.letsBound) { return; }
      root.dataset.letsBound = '1';

      var body = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-body]');
      var select = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-select]');
      var variantInput = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-variant]');
      var ctaPrice = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-cta-price]');
      var types = root.querySelectorAll('[data-lets-po-type]');

      function selectedType() {
        var checked = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-type]:checked');
        return checked ? checked.value : 'onetime';
      }

      function syncType() {
        var subscribing = selectedType() === 'subscribe';

        root.querySelectorAll('[data-lets-po-card]').forEach(function (card) {
          card.classList.toggle('is-selected', card.getAttribute('data-lets-po-card') === selectedType());
        });

        if (body) { body.hidden = !subscribing; }
        // A one-time purchase must NOT carry a selling_plan — Shopify would
        // create a subscription contract for a shopper who did not ask for one.
        if (select) { select.disabled = !subscribing; }
        syncCtaPrice();
      }

      function syncCtaPrice() {
        if (!ctaPrice) { return; }
        if (selectedType() !== 'subscribe') {
          ctaPrice.textContent = ctaPrice.getAttribute('data-onetime-price') || '';
          return;
        }
        // With a cadence picker the price follows the CHOSEN plan, not the lead one.
        var option = select && select.options ? select.options[select.selectedIndex] : null;
        var price = option && option.getAttribute('data-price');
        ctaPrice.textContent = price || ctaPrice.getAttribute('data-sub-price') || '';
      }

      types.forEach(function (input) { input.addEventListener('change', syncType); });
      if (select && select.tagName === 'SELECT') { select.addEventListener('change', syncCtaPrice); }
      syncType();

      // ---- Add to cart WITHOUT leaving the product page ----
      // The <form> POST stays as the no-JS fallback; when JS is available we send
      // the line to /cart/add.js instead, so the shopper keeps their place. The
      // payload is BUILT, not scraped from the form: /cart/add.js would turn any
      // stray field (our own radio, for one) into a line-item property.
      var form = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-form]');
      var cta = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-cta]');
      var afterAdd = root.getAttribute('data-lets-po-after') || 'stay';

      function cartCountRefresh() {
        // Ask the theme to re-read the cart. Themes listen for their own events;
        // between them these cover Dawn and most OS 2.0 themes, and a theme that
        // listens for none simply shows the updated count on the next navigation.
        document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:refresh', { bubbles: true }));
        document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:build', { bubbles: true }));
        if (window.Shopify && window.Shopify.onCartUpdate) {
          try { window.Shopify.onCartUpdate(); } catch (e) { /* theme's own hook */ }
        }
      }

      function openCartDrawer() {
        var drawer = document.querySelector('cart-drawer, #CartDrawer, .drawer--cart, [data-cart-drawer]');
        if (drawer && typeof drawer.open === 'function') { drawer.open(); return true; }

        var toggle = document.querySelector('[data-cart-drawer-toggle], #cart-icon-bubble, .header__icon--cart');
        if (toggle) { toggle.click(); return true; }

        return false;
      }

      if (form && cta) {
        form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
          if (!window.fetch) { return; } // no fetch → let the normal POST happen
          e.preventDefault();

          var subscribing = selectedType() === 'subscribe';
          var item = {
            id: Number(variantInput.value),
            quantity: 1,
          };
          if (subscribing && select && select.value) {
            item.selling_plan = Number(select.value);
          }

          cta.disabled = true;

          fetch('/cart/add.js', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Accept: 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ items: [item] }),
          })
            .then(function (response) {
              return response.json().then(function (data) {
                if (!response.ok) { throw new Error(data.description || data.message || 'add_failed'); }

                return data;
              });
            })
            .then(function () {
              cta.disabled = false;
              cartCountRefresh();

              if (afterAdd === 'cart') { window.location.href = '/cart'; return; }
              if (afterAdd === 'checkout') { window.location.href = '/checkout'; return; }
              if (!openCartDrawer()) {
                // No drawer to open — say plainly that it worked rather than
                // leaving the shopper wondering whether the click registered.
                cta.setAttribute('data-lets-added', '1');
                window.setTimeout(function () { cta.removeAttribute('data-lets-added'); }, 2500);
              }
            })
            .catch(function () {
              cta.disabled = false;
              // Anything unexpected → fall back to the real form POST, which
              // lands on /cart and shows Shopify's own error if there is one.
              form.submit();
            });
        });
      }

      var moreToggle = root.querySelector('[data-lets-po-more]');
      var moreBody = root.querySelector('#lets-po-more');
      if (moreToggle && moreBody) {
        moreToggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var open = moreToggle.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
          moreToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'false' : 'true');
          moreBody.hidden = open;
        });
      }

      // Keep the posted variant in sync with the theme's variant picker, so the
      // cart line is always the variant the shopper is actually looking at.
      document.addEventListener('change', function (e) {
        var input = e.target.closest('select[name="id"], input[name="id"]');
        if (input && input.value && input !== variantInput) { variantInput.value = input.value; }
      });
      document.addEventListener('variant:change', function (e) {
        var variant = e && e.detail && e.detail.variant;
        if (variant && variant.id) { variantInput.value = variant.id; }
      });
    })();
  </script>

{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    No product context (the block was placed outside a product page) — say so in
    the editor instead of rendering nothing, which a merchant reads as "broken".
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="lets-po__hint">
    {{ 'LETS purchase options: this block only renders on a product page. Move it into the product template.' }}
  </p>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "LETS Subscribe & Save",
  "target": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows a subscribe-or-buy-once chooser when this product has a published subscription plan, and a plain one-time card when it does not — so it is safe to add to every product page. It inherits your theme's font and colours by default; set a colour below only where you want it to differ. If your theme already shows its own add-to-cart, hide that one to avoid two buttons."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "default_selection",
      "label": "Pre-selected option",
      "options": [
        { "value": "subscribe", "label": "Subscription" },
        { "value": "onetime", "label": "One-time purchase" }
      ],
      "default": "subscribe"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subscribe_label",
      "label": "Subscription title",
      "default": "Auto Replenish"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "one_time_label",
      "label": "One-time title",
      "default": "Purchase Once"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "badge_text",
      "label": "Badge text",
      "info": "Leave empty to show the saving Shopify calculates, e.g. \"20% OFF\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "badge_off_word",
      "label": "Badge word after the percentage",
      "default": "OFF"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Benefits"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "benefit_1",
      "label": "Benefit 1",
      "info": "Leave empty to show the plan's own delivery cadence."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "benefit_2",
      "label": "Benefit 2",
      "default": "Free shipping"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "benefit_3",
      "label": "Benefit 3",
      "default": "Cancel anytime"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "more_label",
      "label": "\"Read more\" label",
      "default": "Read more"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "more_body",
      "label": "\"Read more\" content",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide the link."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cadence_label",
      "label": "Cadence picker label",
      "default": "Delivery every",
      "info": "Shown only when the product has more than one plan."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Free gift row"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "gift_image",
      "label": "Gift image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gift_tag",
      "label": "Gift tag",
      "default": "Exclusive free gifts"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gift_text",
      "label": "Gift description",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide the whole gift row."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gift_free_label",
      "label": "Gift price label",
      "default": "FREE"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gift_value",
      "label": "Gift value (struck through)",
      "info": "Free text, e.g. $86."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Button"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "button_label",
      "label": "Add-to-cart label",
      "default": "Add to cart"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_price_in_button",
      "label": "Show the price in the button",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sold_out_label",
      "label": "Sold-out label",
      "default": "Sold out"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "after_add",
      "label": "After adding to cart",
      "info": "The item is added without reloading the page.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "stay", "label": "Stay on the page / open cart drawer" },
        { "value": "cart", "label": "Go to the cart" },
        { "value": "checkout", "label": "Go straight to checkout" }
      ],
      "default": "stay"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colours"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Accent (selected border, badge, checks)",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "card_bg",
      "label": "Card background",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "Card border",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "title_color",
      "label": "Titles & prices",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Body text",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "muted_color",
      "label": "Struck-through prices",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "badge_text_color",
      "label": "Badge text",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "gift_tag_bg",
      "label": "Gift tag background",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "gift_tag_color",
      "label": "Gift tag text",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "button_bg",
      "label": "Button background",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "button_fg",
      "label": "Button text",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "corner_radius",
      "label": "Corner radius",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
